      "id": "claim_29158059bb9a48c4bd649826c273c76e",
      "statement": "Caching is central to the library's intended use: a CacheManager hands out Cache instances backed by local-file, Redis, or REST-Redis backends layered according to the CACHE_HIERARCHY variable, and with a fixed seed and temperature identical requests are served from the cache instead of being re-sent to the model, which makes runs reproducible and keeps API cost and latency down.",
